# Rules for Cursor / VS Code Copilot / AI Assistants on PDF Pro project

You MUST follow these rules at all times. Do not wait for the user to remind you.

## Auto-Update & Git Workflow Rule

Whenever you finish modifying the codebase (adding features, fixing bugs, or updating files):
1. **Automatically bump the version in VERSION.txt**:
   - Read the current version from `VERSION.txt`.
   - By default, bump the Patch version (e.g. `1.2.2` -> `1.2.3`). If it is a major feature/refactoring, bump the Minor version (e.g. `1.2.2` -> `1.3.0`).
   - Write the new version back to `VERSION.txt`.
2. **Update CHANGELOG.txt**:
   - Replace the content of `CHANGELOG.txt` with an extremely brief and high-level bullet-pointed summary of the changes (e.g., "- Nâng cấp server", "- Tối ưu trải nghiệm"). DO NOT include any technical details or internal structural descriptions to prevent malicious actors from analyzing the system.
3. **Compile & Package**:
   - Run the packaging script to verify compile and update `AssemblyInfo.cs` and `update-manifest.json`:
     `powershell .\package_project.ps1`
4. **Git Commit & Tag & Push**:
   - Run git commands to commit all changes, tag the commit with the new version, and push:
     ```powershell
     git add .
     git commit -m "Update: [Brief summary] - Version v[New Version]"
     git tag "v[New Version]"
     git push origin master
     git push origin "v[New Version]"
     ```
     *(Pushing the tag is critical because it triggers the GitHub Actions CI/CD to build and publish the release to the update server).*
